{"entryId":"1464","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1464:1","sourceSha256":"5c61027453164a8b81772e4eb37da8b07cb42260f1f324165b0fef33bc1a3140","englishSha256":"d80d6aa9560160354e4624b2d4f6d4469ee92ab7e1b4b372ccad0872b7c569e3","citations":[{"id":"1464:1:citation-01","he":[17,97],"en":[55,58],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_54b.29"},"reference":"Bava Kamma 54b:29","assessment":"The chapter-end question starts on 54b under the name ben Agil in this Bavli edition, and crosses onto 55a.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 54b:29","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_54b.29"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Kamma 55a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_55a.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1464:1:citation-02","he":[99,125],"en":[145,218],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_55a.2"},"reference":"Bava Kamma 55a:2","assessment":"Chiyya directs him to Tanchum on 55a, and the next segment records that he went. The reciprocal Heilprin profile names Agol.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 55a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_55a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Kamma 55a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_55a.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3576:1","target":{"entry":3576,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"1464:1:citation-03","he":[127,174],"en":[219,259],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Yevamot_6.6.3"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Yevamot 6:6:3","assessment":"Jerusalem Yevamot cites Chanina bar Agol in the name of Chizkiyah on a marriage settlement.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Yevamot 6:6:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Yevamot_6.6.3"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The Bavli spells the name Agil, with the question on 54b and Chiyya’s direction and the visit on 55a. The reciprocal Heilprin profile corroborates the visit; the Jerusalem Yevamot witness names bar Agol.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 54b:29","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_54b.29"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Kamma 55a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_55a.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Kamma 55a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_55a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3576:1","target":{"entry":3576,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Yevamot 6:6:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Yevamot_6.6.3"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
